From f2689e1ecd24b4f099eea88c707da481fd5ed613 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:35:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test: show running tests' progress live, and stream it as
 JSON lines

The worker forwards each phase as it starts (setting up the chain,
starting nodes, running, stopping nodes, cleaning up) and each line the
test logs at INFO or above to the runner.

On an interactive terminal, the single status line becomes a live block:
a summary line, then one line per running test with its phase, time so
far and last log line. Results and failure details print above it.

--jsonl-file gets "phase" and "log" events per test. With --jsonl-file=-
standard output carries only the JSON lines, and the console output
(including that of processes the runner starts) goes to standard error,
so a tool can read the stream from a pipe.

